Z||000008||mrfiero||11-06-2001||03:00 AM||||There is a nice 59K mile Indy up on eBay right now.  It is sitting at $2093, which is a great price for a nice Indy.  It looks to be in very nice condition too.<P>High mileage Indy's (like the 108K mile one you looked at) usually are not worth the effort, except for some parts.  The leather seats, leather armrests, leather steering wheel & shifter knobs are very high wear items on Indy's and many people replace them with the "regular" Fiero parts.  This greatly reduces any intrinsic value an Indy has, so many times you over pay for a car that just isn't worth it.<P>Anyways.....go here <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=597429648&r=0&t=0&showTutorial=0&ed=1005192156&indexURL=0&rd=1" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=597429648&r=0&t=0&showTutorial=0&ed=1005192156&indexURL=0&rd=1</A>   to check it out.<P>BTW.......I live in the Denver area (where this car is located) and can look at it for you if you are interested.  LMK.<P>||||reg||1
